---
description: Use SCORM Player's local MCP tools and Cursor browser for SCORM lesson review, annotation pins, and live source verification.
alwaysApply: false
---

When reviewing SCORM lessons or acting on SCORM Player pins, follow the bundled scormplayer-review skill. Prefer MCP tools for player identity, revision and fresh pins, and Cursor's available browser tools for rendered navigation and verification. Discover WebMCP only when the browser advertises it; otherwise use the visible browser controls and DOM. Never pretend server MCP tools can see the active browser page, unsaved SCORM calls, or playback state.

Use the user's authoring source, not a cached ZIP extraction. Keep the selected player ID and observed course revision on scoped calls. Inspect desktop/tablet and larger screens after changes. Resolve pins only after verification within the user's requested scope. The optional MCP Apps pin panel works progressively: use its structured result or copyable request when rich UI or messaging is unavailable.

Prefer the native `scormplayer-cursor` plugin's tools over a separately imported Claude `scormplayer` package, which may be an older version. Use one server's owned session consistently; never start one session through each duplicate provider.
